; A journal that does NOT balance, so the grouped balance sheet's check line has
; something to find.
;
; It lives under an `errors/` directory for the same reason
; `fixtures/corpus/errors/` does: the fixture-tree sweeps
; (`tests/diagnostics.rs::the_whole_fixtures_tree_is_diagnostic_free`) assert
; that every journal hledger ACCEPTS produces no diagnostics, and skip any
; directory called `errors`. This file is the counter-example those sweeps must
; not trip over.
;
; The second transaction posts $100.00 out and $90.00 in, with BOTH amounts
; written explicitly so nothing is inferred to paper over the gap. hledger
; refuses the file outright:
;
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/errors/bs-unbalanced.journal bal
;   hledger: Error: …:35-37:
;     This transaction is unbalanced.
;     The real postings' sum should be 0 but is: $10.00
;
; Ledgeline opens it anyway — an unbalanced transaction is a diagnostic here, not
; a parse error (see `parse::check_transaction_balances`) — so the report has to
; be the thing that says so. `A − L − E` comes out as exactly `$10.00`: the same
; residual, in the same commodity, arrived at from the other end.

account assets:bank        ; type: A
account liabilities:cc     ; type: L
account equity:opening     ; type: E
account income:fees        ; type: R
account expenses:food      ; type: X

2026-01-01 opening balance
    assets:bank                $1,000.00
    equity:opening            $-1,000.00

2026-02-01 short by ten
    expenses:food                $100.00
    assets:bank                  $-90.00
